# kk: A few convenience changes for debugging
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44565 state=merged
# ### What does this MR do and why?

The MR has a couple of changes to help with debugging:
- It doesn't create counter pools and instead just writes zeroes for Vulkan timestamp. Not great but it only does that if capturing is enabled and the Metal capture layer refuses to work completely otherwise. At least I put in a warning when a query pool is created.
- Don't immediately start capturing at launch unless `MESA_KK_GPU_CAPTURE_IMMEDIATELY=1` is also set.
- Support controling capturing via Vulkan debug utils messages: `capture-marker,begin_capture` and `capture-marker,end-capture`. Renderdoc uses those markers and DXVK uses them.
- Push debug groups to the command buffer if there's no active encoder. The debug groups of DXVK got lost without this.

Some other things we could do in the future:
- Add in the ability to capture specific frames into Kosmickrisp. That would ofc be tricky because there could be multiple swapchains but 'best effort' would probably be good enough for the vast majority of cases.
- Move existing Metal capture files out of the way because the capture layer refuses to use any other filename than `processname.mtlcapture`.
--- docs/drivers/kosmickrisp.rst
+++ docs/drivers/kosmickrisp.rst
@@ -76,7 +76,8 @@ Environment variables
 KosmicKrisp specific environment variables:
 
 - ``MESA_KK_DEBUG``: ``msl`` to log all generated Metal Shading Language (MSL) shaders. ``force_robustness`` to force robustness on all shaders.
-- ``MESA_KK_GPU_CAPTURE``: Starts Metal capture at device create and ends it at device destroy. Set to ``1`` to activate.
+- ``MESA_KK_GPU_CAPTURE``: Enables Metal capture, can be controlled using debug utils labels or using ``MESA_KK_GPU_CAPTURE_IMMEDIATELY``. Set to ``1`` to activate.
+- ``MESA_KK_GPU_CAPTURE_IMMEDIATELY``: Starts Metal capture at device creation and ends it at device destruction. Set to ``1`` to activate.
 - ``MESA_KK_GPU_CAPTURE_DIRECTORY``: Metal capture will be saved to the specified directory. Defaults to Xcode if no path is provided.
 - ``MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS``: Provide ``all`` to disable all workarounds. Otherwise, provide a comma separated list to disable wanted workarounds e.g. ``1,3,4`` to disable workaround 1, 3 and 4.
 - ``MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL``: Enables advertising experimental features which may not provide full correctness or may negatively impact performance when enabled. Provide ``all`` to advertise all listed features.

